  "reason": "Existing evidence shows that using transformer aggregation and weighted fusion with scvi_n200 RNA and imagenet_vit_l image encoders achieves high accuracy (0.7249). This experiment tests whether replacing the RNA encoder with pca_n2000 (a simpler PCA-based method) maintains performance while reducing training cost. It clarifies the importance of RNA encoder complexity and balances exploration of encoder choices with exploitation of proven components. Expected cost is similar to config_025 (3.60 GPU hours) but with a simpler RNA encoder, making it a cost-effective way to validate architectural decisions."
